text:
harper: Starting a focused relnotes + changelog thread for the docs deploy. Goals: final bullets, a short migration note for routing policy v2, and a lightweight code-sample inventory sweep. Opening draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5060

noah: I'll run a quick grep for old client patterns and anchor renames. If we can batch fixes that would reduce churn for translators.

keiko: Heads-up: fr/zh translations flagged placeholders not normalized in a few code blocks. INTL ticket queued.

sam: Found about 18 files using `Client.create` or `new Client()` variants. I'll standardize them to `const client = new RedwoodClient(...)` + `await client.responses.create(...)`. Will include try/catch in examples that show network errors.

harper: Perfect. Also add a small Known Issue: "Embeddings streaming may return intermittent 403s on long multi-chunk uploads. Workaround: set batch_size=1 and enable prefix_cache." Keiko, can you paste the repro ID?

keiko: Repro attached in PR comment: EVAL-2024-10-11. I'll also include a tiny troubleshooting snippet for the docs.

noah: I found two stale anchors in /guides/quantize and /guides/migrate-0.9. I'll open a redirect PR and list files touched so relnotes can link the fix.

docs-bot: docs-ci queued for PR #5061 (redirects) -- status: running

sam: Draft JS example for relnotes (final API style):
```javascript
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
try {
  const resp = await client.responses.create({
    model: "redwood-kestrel-1",
    input: "Summarize the changes in this release",
  });
  console.log(resp.output_text);
} catch (err) {
  console.error("Request failed", err);
}
```

keiko: Style note: docs prefer double quotes and minimal error-handling examples; I'll run a lint pass after Sam's commit. Also tagging INTL-1012 for the fr/zh placeholder normalization.

harper: Migration blurb for Dedicated (2 lines) suggestion: "Routing policy v2 changes fallback ordering to prefer lower-latency regional variants. Customers pinning model IDs should verify rollouts after upgrade and consult SE for assisted migrations." Thoughts?

noah: Good. Add link from Dedicated docs to the top-level changelog so customers see it immediately. I'll include the direct anchor in the redirect PR.

docs-bot: PR #5061 build succeeded; redirects merged

sam: Pushed the snippet standardization commit to the relnotes PR. Replaced constructor calls and updated examples across quickstart, guides, and SDK pages. Listing touched files in PR description.

keiko: Intl check: placeholders fixed in most files, two left in `/docs/guides/embed-stream` that need translator confirmation. INTL-1012 updated.

harper: Cutoff reminder: localization freeze at 2024-09-30 23:59 UTC. Target publish: 2024-10-08 16:00 PT. After freeze, small typo fixes only.

noah: I'll open a tiny follow-up PR for the Dedicated page to link the changelog and call out the routing-policy note. CI green.

sam: Added Known Issue + troubleshooting snippet to the relnotes PR body and linked EVAL-2024-10-11. Also included the JS + Python snippets for translators to review.

keiko: Intl team will confirm by EOD tomorrow. Once confirmed I'll drop the thumbs-up in the PR.

harper: Thanks everyone. Once intl thumbs-up is in, I'll do a final proof and ship the relnotes branch. :rocket:
